// Example subc daemon config entry for the ai-provider-quota module.
//
// Install: merge this `modules` entry into your real subc config at
//   $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cortexkit/subc.jsonc   (default: ~/.config/cortexkit/subc.jsonc)
// and point `program` at your built binary (cargo build --release →
// target/release/ck-insula). On its next start, the ck-subc daemon spawns +
// supervises it.
//
// The daemon appends `--subc <connection-file>` and injects the SUBC_MODULE_ID env
// var itself — do NOT add those to args/env here. The map KEY ("ai-provider-quota")
// is the module id the daemon registers it under.
//
// The key and the binary deliberately differ. The repository and its binary were
// renamed to insula; the module id was not, because every other repository that
// calls this module names it by that id, and such a reference does not block a
// rename — it breaks when one lands. Changing the key here renames the module as
// far as the daemon is concerned, and every caller loses its route.
{
  "version": 1,
  "modules": {
    "ai-provider-quota": {
      "program": "/abs/path/to/insula/target/release/ck-insula",
      "args": [],
      "env": {},
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
